<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00395</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a7d36700-2a38-46f8-ab3d-4d10d0927999</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="1f209805-d7b2-47b1-8d9f-e26f07909497" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following points is the solution to the system of equations that is graphed?
          <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_10_01.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((20,0)\)</para>
            <para>\((0,20)\)</para>
            <para>\(45,0)\)</para>
            <para>\((5,15)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The two points intersect at the point \((5,15)\) so that is the solution of the system.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \((5, 15)\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="7b734813-1789-4f31-8e93-148a0efa37d1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following points is the solution to the system of equations that is graphed?
          <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_10_02.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((5,2)\)</para>
            <para>\((2,5)\)</para>
            <para>\((8,0)\)</para>
            <para>\((5.2,0)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The two points intersect at the point \((5, 2)\) so that is the solution of the system.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \((5, 2)\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="4ce91135-8284-4df5-b5c7-bd005f637908" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What two equations are represented by the graph? Select <emphasis>two</emphasis>.
          <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_10_03.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The system of equations includes \(y=\frac12x-1\) and \(y=4x-2\).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.1. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is the system of equations includes \(y=\frac12x-1\) and \(y=4x-2\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="357cb642-ec02-46bd-8cfd-1e9a42dc417a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What two equations are represented by the graph? Select<emphasis> two</emphasis>.
          <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_10_04.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The system of equations includes \(y=x-1\) and \(y=3x-2\).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is the system of equations includes \(y=x-1\) and \(y=3x-2\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <para>For questions 5 – 8, use the following scenario and matching table.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>A streaming service has two different membership plans. Option A charges $10 per month plus $5 for each movie. Option B charges $20 a month then $2 a movie.</quote>
      </para>
      <table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
        <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>Number of movies in a month, \(x\).</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>0</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>1</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>2</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>3</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>4</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
          </row>
        <row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>Option A</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>10</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>15</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>20</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>25</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>30</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <para>Option B</para>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>20</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>22</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>24</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>26</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>28</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="a77aa2bc-c28c-4a82-bce2-f92d629bcdf3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
            <para> What is the \(y\)-intercept for Option A and Option B? </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: 10\\ Option\;\ B: 20\)</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: 20\\ Option\;\ B: 10\)</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: 5\\ Option\;\ B: 2\)</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: 2\\ Option\;\ B: 5\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercepts are Option A = 10 and Option B = 20.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is the \(y\)-intercepts are Option A = 10 and Option B = 20.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d22fc5ee-0e88-4a81-a45f-ed0a3765594e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
            <para>What is the slope of Option A and Option B? </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: \frac{52}x=9\\ Option\;\ B: m =\frac 12\)</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: m=2\\ Option\;\ B: m =5\)</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: m =\frac12\\ Option\;\ B: m =\frac15\)</para>
            <para>\(Option\;\ A: m =5\\ Option\;\ B: m =2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The slopes are Option A = 5 and Option B = 2.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is the slopes are Option A = 5 and Option B = 2.. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f1b30519-391e-4428-9902-f50ed11086aa" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
            <para>What is the equation of Option A?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=10x+5\)</para>
            <para>\(y=5x-10\)</para>
            <para>\(y=5x+10\)</para>
            <para>\(y=10x-5\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The equation of the line for Option A is \(y=5x+10\).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is the equation of the line for Option A is \(y=5x+10\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="79950d77-b1c9-45cf-aa22-18aa372b6184" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
            <para>What is the equation of Option B?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=5x+20\)</para>
            <para>\(y=2x+20\)</para>
            <para>\(y=5x+10\)</para>
            <para>\(y=2x+10\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The equation of the line for Option A is \(y=5x+10\).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is the equation of the line for Option A is \(y=5x+10\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <para>For questions 9 - 12, use the following situation and graph.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>A family buys a total of 32 tickets at a carnival. Ride tickets cost $1.50 each and food tickets cost $3.25 each. The family pays a total of $90 for the tickets. The situation is graphed below.</quote>
        <quote>
          <figure>
            <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_04_10_05.jpg"/>
            </media>
          </figure>
        </quote>
        <quote>The \(x\)-axis represents the number of ride tickets and the \(y\)-axis represents the number of food tickets.</quote>
      </para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="e7633643-d341-4b95-9151-a83dc6c45559" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which line depicts the equation that represents the statement “A family buys a total of 32 tickets at a carnival”?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution/>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d676f4bf-d5af-4c8f-865e-448984b5155a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The remaining line represents the statements “Ride tickets cost $1.50 each and food tickets cost $3.25 each. The family pays a total of $90 for the tickets.” Which equation corresponds to these statements and the remaining line?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>1.50x + 3.25y = 90</para>
            <para>3.25x + 1.50y = 90</para>
            <para>(1.50 + 3.25)x = 90y</para>
            <para>(1.50 + 3.25)y = 90x</para>
          </problem>
          <solution/>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="7984860e-cdd8-4802-aa9d-f49cb162dbc9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the approximate number of ride tickets the family purchased?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>32</para>
            <para>60</para>
            <para>7</para>
            <para>24</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The two lines intersect at approximately \((8, 24)\) and the \(x\)-value represents the number of ride tickets which is 8.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.4. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 8.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="63f44116-78d4-4a5c-93fb-b8834627837e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the approximate number of food tickets the family purchased?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>32</para>
            <para>60</para>
            <para>7</para>
            <para>24</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The two lines intersect at (8,24) and the y-value represents the number of food tickets which is 24.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.4. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 24.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>